Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 13 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 2, row A10): THE TRIPWIRE OF B1862 READS ITS OWN
 ARC'S PAGE

A reader's check of main's answers at Review 80 (agy-002's; row A10, not checked by main). The third part of
the reader's finding was answered wrongly: the test main named reads one sentence of B1862's page and looks
for no old form, and the page is exempt from the tripwire, so an old form added to it passes both. The
fourth part was not answered.

Made again here, in a small repository: the page as it stands with the lemma of E4 added and no correction
beside it; with the count of E13 once more; with the sentence of E11. As the tripwire read until this patch,
nothing of the arc was read, and none of the three gave a hit.

The mend. The tripwire reads the arc's page and its verdict file. It does not read the folder of the lock
itself, which plants the old forms to show that it sees them. The page quotes two old forms in blocks that
do not hold their correction (its table of what the audit found): one of E13 and one of E3. They are held by
count, as found on 2026-11-12: one more of either, or one of any other finding, is reported, and the lock
asks that the table be shortened when the page no longer holds them.

The planted cases, in the patch's own test: each of the three added sentences is reported as one more than
is held. The same lemma with its correction in its block is not reported.

NOT BUILT: the fourth part of the reader's finding. Main's line says that it was not answered and does not
say what it is; it is in the reader's file, which is read through a mask.

The lock passes: 15 tests. Every gate passes but the count of landings.
Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors by the session that wrote it.
